  "worked_solution": "Since the line $y=3$ is a horizontal line, a perpendicular line would need to be vertical. So, the perpendicular line must take the form $x=k$ for some value of $k.$\n\nThe perpendicular line needs to go through the point $(-4,-3),$ which has an $x$-coordinate of $-4.$ So, the perpendicular line is $x=-4.$",
